.TH CODEX-USAGE-TRAY 1 "July 2026" "codex-usage-tray 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codex-usage-tray \- display OpenAI Codex usage limits in the Ubuntu system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codex-usage-tray
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B codex-usage-tray
starts an unofficial GTK 3 AppIndicator application that reads account state
and usage limits from the local OpenAI Codex app-server. It displays the
remaining allowance in the Ubuntu GNOME top panel.
.PP
OpenAI Codex must be installed separately. If Codex is signed out, the tray
displays a sign-in-required state and offers a Sign in to Codex... action that
starts the official Codex-managed ChatGPT browser flow. Users may also run
.B codex login
in a terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/codex-usage-tray.desktop
System-wide autostart entry used to launch the application after login.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3, GTK 3, PyGObject, Ayatana AppIndicator, and OpenAI Codex.
